<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	The Keychain on iOS refuses every request from a process that carries no
	`application-identifier`, answering errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018). The
	smoke test builds a bare bundle, so it has to be signed with the same
	entitlement Xcode would otherwise add on its own, or the node cannot reach
	its own state store and never starts.

	This is also the answer to whether a shipping build needs anything extra: it
	does not. Xcode grants `application-identifier` and a matching
	`keychain-access-groups` entry to every signed app, for a free Apple ID
	account as much as a paid one. Only an unsigned harness has to say so.
	-->
	<key>application-identifier</key>
	<string>app.camellia.mobile.smoke</string>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>app.camellia.mobile.smoke</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
